cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these study notes, please cite them using the metadata below."
title: "Study Notes on Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction (2nd Ed.)"
abstract: >-
  Independent personal study notes accompanying Richard S. Sutton and Andrew G.
  Barto's Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction (2nd ed., MIT Press, 2018; 2020 corrected reprint).
  Written in original prose across all 13 chapters with original Python
  implementations and programmatically generated conceptual diagrams, built as
  a Quarto book (HTML, PDF, EPUB 3.3) with a native MathJax Anki cloze deck.
  Intended as a study companion and not a substitute for the textbook.
authors:
